### +1HP — Epistemic Instrumental Zoning Utility

Implementation Standard: EIZU-001 Architecture: Epistemic Articulacy · Orthographic Integrity · Cryptologic Classification · Geographic Information Systems (GIS) Application: Land Use · Zoning · Resource Management · Geospatial Documentation · Institutional Oversight

### I. Governing implementation principle

The Zoning Utility converts geographic information into a structured, color-coded, spatially identifiable, and auditable classification system.

The implementation must preserve five independent dimensions:

* Geographic identity — Where is the designated area?

* Land-use identity — What activity or use is classified?

* Chromatic identity — What color or pattern represents it?

* Regulatory identity — What rules govern the designation?

* Epistemic identity — What evidence establishes the classification?

The governing sequence is:

\\text{Geography}
\\rightarrow \\text{Classification}
\\rightarrow \\text{Orthography}
\\rightarrow \\text{Colorization}
\\rightarrow \\text{Verification}
\\rightarrow \\text{Audit}

