### X. HI / ME / LO — Zoning utility interface

The three-tier architecture provides an interface hierarchy.

| Tier | Interface                         | Information                              |
| ---- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| HI   | Governance and oversight          | Regulations, legal authority, evidence   |
| ME   | Classification and interpretation | Land-use categories, maps, colors        |
| LO   | Data and telemetry                | Coordinates, records, hashes, timestamps |

### Visual arrangement

* HI: Prime Ivory header and governing reference.

* ME: Color-coded GIS map and classification panels.

* LO: Obsidian data containers, identifiers, and audit telemetry.

* Footer: Chromatic legend, source references, verification status.

* Anchor: Geographic reference and jurisdictional boundaries.

